{
  "description": "Decision-layer fixtures for decideBash: SC20's named-path rule (a write-class piece naming a primary-checkout path is denied from any cwd, while a read-class piece naming the same path and the outside-any-repo uncertain class stay allowed), the destination scope of that rule (a write command's read sources, verb words, flags, and non-path flag values -- a git commit message, a cp source -- are not write targets and are left unjudged, so SC16's `git commit -m \"$(date)\"` is allowed from a worktree and denied from a primary checkout), SC15's digest-verified provisioned-CLI allowance (three verbs, no retarget, keyed on binary identity supplied as argv), and the membership walk's indifference to whether a write target already exists (a target that is itself a file or a device node makes its own `.git` probe an ENOTDIR, which answers the membership question rather than clouding it, so an existing-file write earns the same verdict as a new-path one -- while a genuine lstat failure anywhere on the climb still denies). The loader builds one fixed hermetic topology per case: primary checkout /repo, linked worktree /repo/wt, an already-existing tracked.md in each, a device node at /dev/null, provisioned CLI at /plugin-data/bin/git-tools. arg_path/arg_digest default to the correct provisioned path and the sha256 of the binary's bytes; 'omit' passes an empty argv parameter, 'wrong' passes a valid-but-mismatched digest, and a literal overrides. bin_present=false withholds the binary so it cannot be re-hashed. err_at makes one path's lstat fail indeterminately.",
